# Site navigation

The global nav is defined in **one place** and copied into every page by a build script.

## Source files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `components/site-nav.html` | Nav + mobile menu markup (root-relative URLs: `/about`, `/#contact`, etc.) |
| `css/site-nav.css` | Nav styles (transparent until scroll, mobile overlay) |
| `js/site-nav.js` | Scroll `.scrolled`, hamburger, smooth in-page anchors |

## After editing the nav

1. Change `components/site-nav.html`, `css/site-nav.css`, and/or `js/site-nav.js` as needed.
2. Run **`npm run build:nav`** to inline nav HTML into all pages between `<!-- LINKPRO_NAV_START -->` and `<!-- LINKPRO_NAV_END -->`.
3. Commit the component **and** the updated HTML files.

To register a new page, add it to `activeByFile` in `scripts/build-nav.js`, add the markers + `/css/site-nav.css` + `/js/site-nav.js` to the page, then run `npm run build:nav`.

## New pages

- Use the homepage nav pattern only (flat links, no dropdowns).
- Checkout-style light pages: `body class="nav-surface-light"` for a solid nav bar at the top.
